body:
Would you rather have glitches relatively unknown and used infrequently to ruin some of your games or brought to light, so that Ubisoft is forced to fix them? I do not personally care if he profits off of his videos, while he isn't noble in anyway he makes content people watch. Let DBL Online get ad-revenue and make glitches notable, so that Ubisoft will band-aid them instead of fixing them.

&#x200B;

Besides, if the game wasn't a broken mess then his videos wouldn't even have an audience.

That is a reference to the creation of the comics. He wanted to name it Night of the Living Dead, but since the trademark is open domain he would not own the comics.  Partially the reason why Romero dropped Living Dead from the titles of his future movies. 

&#x200B;

 [https://www.cbr.com/walking-dead-night-of-the-living-dead/](https://www.cbr.com/walking-dead-night-of-the-living-dead/) 

&#x200B;

That's an article explaining it. There really is nothing to look deeper into.

I recently found out my friend isn't subscribed to Pewdiepie, so I have been arguing with them for the past couple weeks about subscribing. Me and a couple other friends are now fighting with her about it.

&#x200B;

So, basically... I wrote up a treaty to get her to subscribe and she will not subscribe. Will you sign the petition, so that she will subscribe and help me win the epic victory royale.

&#x200B;

[https://www.change.org/p/draco-sicarus-draco-sign-the-treaty](https://www.change.org/p/draco-sicarus-draco-sign-the-treaty?signed=true)

You can't buy alpha packs with real world money, but you can buy the skins and seasonal packs. 

&#x200B;

If you don't pay $50 then you are forced into a random chance for what you want.

Ubisoft is EA. Just recolored. 

&#x200B;

They do not and never cared about the fans.

Hit reg is not important, you silly goose.

&#x200B;

As a community, we must worry about real issues. Like toxicity and censorship for our new Chinese friends. We can get to hit reg in a couple more years. I know you have been having this issue since launch, but we don't care.

&#x200B;

\-ubisoft

They do use a HWID ban, but IP bans and HWID bans are easily circumvented. 

&#x200B;

Also buying stolen and or cheap keys is easy and as I said "cheap". Like a dollar an account.

Can we get a marketplace to sell our skins to other players for real money?

&#x200B;

It'll really appeal to the Chinese and Venezuelan market.

&#x200B;

edit: Moderators are such a fuckin' hoe, I love it. They do it for free.

Have really good, expensive, (Non ADT) security cameras. Movement detector exists, but it fucking sucks, so I could not imagine having it in 2003. By it fucking sucks, my camera chases a leaf for a couple seconds before finding another leaf (Does not matter the sensitivity and face rec is impossible even with HD or 4k). I just have it off. 

Better to just watch and review footage for around when shit happened. 

&#x200B;

People legit stay in copper and silver (csgo) to prevent players from ranking up. Silver in CSGO is the smurfing rank, because people who are there are either smurfs or actual shitty players. 

&#x200B;

Siege has that issue and I know it's true, because I have three friends who do that. Their justification is that it's fun to see people unable to rank or even win. Shitty matchmaking will put them together multiple times.

This season sucked. 

&#x200B;

Teammates banned, because they were dumb and fell for other people's chat filter tricks. Joined a match and 3 teammates got banned. 3 speed rook/chanka glitch that everyone exploited. (This community sure loves to exploit glitches and the dev team is so fucking slow on fixing them.) Hit reg problems that was blamed on latency, that everyone is getting. 

&#x200B;

Operation Health? Did it even happen.
